pica-pica (0.9.0dev-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Audio/video calls: new build dependencies on FFmpeg (libavcodec,
    libavdevice, libavformat, libavutil, libswresample, libswscale),
    webrtc-audio-processing for acoustic echo cancellation, ALSA,
    libpulse for PulseAudio/PipeWire device enumeration, and
    libva/EGL/GL/X11 for VAAPI accelerated encoding, decoding and
    rendering
  * The echo canceller needs webrtc-audio-processing 1.x or newer, for
    AEC3. The 0.3 that Ubuntu 24.04 still ships predates it, so the
    build dependency is versioned and 24.04 needs a backport
  * Build-depend on pkg-config, sqlite3 and zlib1g-dev, which configure
    has always required but which were only pulled in indirectly
  * Configure VAAPI, its X11 rendering path and PulseAudio device
    enumeration explicitly instead of relying on autodetection
  * pica-client: recommend va-driver-all, depend on openssl - the
    command line tool is used to generate keys and certificates
  * Move to debhelper compat 13, declared through debhelper-compat in
    Build-Depends rather than debian/compat, and drop the now redundant
    autotools-dev build dependency
  * pica-node: install the manual pages from the staged build tree
    rather than listing them in debian/pica-node.manpages. Compat 13
    makes dh_missing fatal and dh_installman reject a page that is both
    staged and listed, and "make install" already stages both pages

 -- Anton Sviridenko <anton@picapica.im>  Fri, 28 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0400

pica-pica (0.7.1-1) unstable; urgency=low

